      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To find the largest 4-digit integer that is congruent to \\(15 \\pmod{22}\\), we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the largest 4-digit integer.\n2. Determine the largest 4-digit integer that is congruent to 15 modulo 22.\n3. Express the solution using modular arithmetic.\n\nThe largest 4-digit integer is 9999. We need to find \\( n \\) such that \\( n \\equiv 15 \\pmod{22} \\) and \\( n \\leq 9999 \\).\n\nTo find \\( n \\), we can use the concept of congruences. We start by solving the congruence:\n\\[ n = 22k + 15 \\]\nfor some integer \\( k \\). We need to find the largest \\( k \\) such that \\( n \\leq 9999 \\):\n\\[ 22k + 15 \\leq 9999 \\]\n\\[ 22k \\leq 9984 \\]\n\\[ k \\leq \\frac{9984}{22} \\]\n\\[ k \\leq 453 \\]\n\nSo, the largest integer \\( k \\) is 453. Substituting \\( k = 453 \\) into the equation for \\( n \\), we get:\n\\[ n = 22 \\cdot 453 + 15 \\]\n\\[ n = 9966 + 15 \\]\n\\[ n = 9981 \\]\n\nTherefore, the largest 4-digit integer that is congruent to \\(15 \\pmod{22}\\) is \\(\\boxed{9981}\\).",
